{"name":"Cider Mill","hex":"#938a43","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cider","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic, often sparkling (carbonated) beverage made from fermented apples.","This or any similar alcoholic drink made from similar fruit, such as pears."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cider"},{"term":"mill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grinding apparatus for substances such as grains, seeds, etc. (Some are small and simple, and some are large and complex.)","The building housing such a grinding apparatus; also, any similar building that houses a similarly material activity (such as weaving, fulling, dying, etc.); the place of business comprising such a building and its outbuildings and grounds."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grind or otherwise process in a mill or other machine.","To shape, polish, dress or finish using a machine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cider mill","blocks":[{"text":"A cider mill, also known as a cidery, is the location and equipment used to crush apples into apple juice for use in making apple cider, hard cider, applejack, apple wine, pectin and other products derived from apples. More specifically, it refers to a device used to crush or grind apples as part of the overall juice production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Cider_making_Jersey.jpg/330px-Cider_making_Jersey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cider_mill"},{"title":"Cider","blocks":[{"text":"Cider is an alcoholic beverage made from the fermented juice of apples. The juice of most varieties of apple can be used to make cider, but cider apples are most desirable. The addition of sugar or extra fruit before a second fermentation increases the ethanol content of the resulting beverage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Midwest_hard_cider.jpg/330px-Midwest_hard_cider.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cider"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Golden_Gate_Park_-_Apple_Press_Monument_02-2.jpg/500px-Golden_Gate_Park_-_Apple_Press_Monument_02-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Golden_Gate_Park_-_Apple_Press_Monument_02-2.jpg/1280px-Golden_Gate_Park_-_Apple_Press_Monument_02-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Golden_Gate_Park_-_Apple_Press_Monument_02-2.jpg/500px-Golden_Gate_Park_-_Apple_Press_Monument_02-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apple Press Monument (a relic of the Mid-Winter Fair, 1894, still in its original location), Music Concourse, Golden Gate Park, San Francisco, California, USA","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGolden_Gate_Park_-_Apple_Press_Monument_02-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Sagarrak_zanpatzen.jpg/500px-Sagarrak_zanpatzen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Sagarrak_zanpatzen.jpg/500px-Sagarrak_zanpatzen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASagarrak_zanpatzen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Fa%C3%AEs%27sie_d%27Cidre_2009_27.jpg/500px-Fa%C3%AEs%27sie_d%27Cidre_2009_27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Fa%C3%AEs%27sie_d%27Cidre_2009_27.jpg/1280px-Fa%C3%AEs%27sie_d%27Cidre_2009